      "name": "disabled text",
      "fg": "fg-disabled",
      "bg": "bg",
      "min": 3.0,
      "note": "WCAG 2.1 SC 1.4.3 EXEMPTS disabled components, and this check used to take the exemption \u2014 min 0.0. That is how --fg-disabled sat at 1.80:1 in the light theme, which is not 'muted', it is invisible. A disabled button whose label cannot be read is one you cannot decide about: you cannot tell what enabling it would do. 3.0 is the floor for non-text and large text, and it keeps 'disabled' legible while still clearly distinct from --fg-secondary (5.02:1 light, 8.84:1 dark). It also removes an ASYMMETRY: the two themes were 1.80 and 3.17, so the same token meant two different degrees of 'off'."
